      "title": "Addressing High Latency and Timeout Issues in Customer Portal",
      "content_summary": "Provides a general overview of troubleshooting slow response times, HTTP 504 errors, and database timeouts in the Customer Portal, focusing on resource constraints and third-party dependencies.",
      "content_body": "When users report slow page loads or intermittent HTTP 504 errors, first check the Admin Console for resource usage spikes, particularly CPU and memory during peak hours. Database query timeouts are often caused by resource exhaustion rather than code inefficiency; verify if query performance degrades only under heavy load. In some cases, slow mobile app performance is linked to third-party service failures or rate limits, so review external API response times. If the issue stems from a known product limitation or as-designed behavior, document this for customer expectation management. For persistent issues, consider requesting a capacity increase or adjusting rate limits after engaging the vendor for deeper analysis."
